WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.230
A car hits a bump in the road.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.220
A spring in its suspension takes the jolt.

3
00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.770
With too little damping, the car
keeps bouncing long after the bump.

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:16.070
So engineers add a shock absorber: a
damper that forces oil through small holes.

5
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.180
Heavy doors get dampers too,
so they close without slamming.

6
00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.120
But how much damping is just right?

7
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:27.360
In this mission, you'll drive a row
of pendulums with one heavy one,

8
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.520
and see which swings hardest.

9
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.850
Then you'll track where the energy goes,
as each swing ends up smaller than the

10
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.960
last.

11
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.730
Your mission: find out how
much damping is just right,

12
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.970
and explain why.
